@@ -108,6 +108,8 @@ The Mac app (Electron, `desktop/`) loads this same dashboard and gives it a brid
 
 "This restart is mine" (the banner's "Restarting anyscribe's engine.", and no outage) is true only while this page's own Restart engine or removal call is in flight: a module variable, not storage, because the app reloads the page only once the engine runs again.
 
+A page that has seen the engine leave running is **doomed**: the app will replace it. `desktop.ts` sets the flag from the first status read and from any status that is not running, and never resets it. Two things read it: the queue's start gate (a doomed page starts no waiting file; the reloaded page does) and the startup recovery claim. Startup recovery resolves only the removal note present when the page loaded (`noteAtLoad`, its `at` checked again just before anything is cleared or claimed), and the Terminal card waits for it.
+
 **The reload after every restart.** The app loads the dashboard's `/` again each time the engine returns to running (2c-app `main.js`, the `loadURL` in the engine status handler). A restart keeps the port, so the page's origin and its storage survive; anything that must outlive a restart is written to storage before the reload can happen:
 - the outage note (`OUTAGE` in sessionStorage, `{job, at}`): written when the engine stops by itself; the reloaded page shows "Running again" naming the job once;
 - the queue of dropped and Dock files (sessionStorage), written inside the callback because the preload acknowledges a file as soon as it returns. A file starts only while the engine reads running and the page is idle or done; it leaves the queue only once the engine accepted it. On a failure it stays at the head and the error screen is the pause (Try again resubmits it; New drops it only when it is the one that failed);
diff --git a/docs/building/journal/2026-11-20-mac-app-2c-ui.md b/docs/building/journal/2026-11-20-mac-app-2c-ui.md
index e790cec..d08e351 100644
--- a/docs/building/journal/2026-11-20-mac-app-2c-ui.md
+++ b/docs/building/journal/2026-11-20-mac-app-2c-ui.md
@@ -89,3 +89,28 @@ Documented limits (not built):
 - Files waiting in Up next are lost if anyscribe quits before they start.
 - Real Electron reload timing and sessionStorage across `loadURL`: no stub
   proves them; they stay a check on a Mac.
+
+## Round 3 (review: NOT YET and CONDITIONAL)
+
+Two gaps in round 2's design, closed by two rules:
+- **A doomed page starts nothing new.** Every return to running reloads the
+  dashboard, so a page that has seen the engine leave running will be
+  replaced. Without the flag, the old page could start a waiting file just
+  before its reload, so the file ran twice or ran unseen. The flag has two
+  readers only: the queue start and the startup recovery claim.
+- **An async callback acts only on the state it started from.** The removal
+  note is read once at page load. Startup recovery resolves only that note,
+  so a slow recovery read can no longer clear the note of a Remove clicked
+  meanwhile.
+
+Also: the cleanup checklist shows the bridge's reason; files waiting for the
+engine are named in the idle, completed and cancelled views; the stub's
+removal now settles after "running", with the reload 300 ms later.
+
+Documented limits (not built):
+- A crash during a queued file's POST can run that file twice.
+- A click on a doomed page in the instant before its reload.
+- A removal result is lost if anyscribe quits before a page claims it
+  (`lastRemoval` is in the app's memory only).
+- A second Remove overwrites an unclaimed note.
+- Real Electron timing stays a check on a Mac.
